Article 5 (Criteria and procedures for selection of assessment bodies)
The selection criteria for an assessment body under Article 10 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "assessment body") are as follows:
It shall be a legal person;
Its selection as an assessment body shall not have been revoked within the last 2 years;
It shall employ at least 5 full-time professional personnel who meet the requirements specified in Appendix 1;
It shall have the operational and management capabilities and technical and physical capabilities necessary to conduct assessments;
It shall be able to ensure independence, objectivity, impartiality, and reliability in conducting assessments.
Details, including assessment items and assessment methods, to confirm compliance with the criteria under paragraph (1) 4 and 5 shall be prescribed by Ministerial Decree of Science and ICT.
A person that seeks to be selected as an assessment body shall submit an application for selection in the form prescribed by Ministerial Decree of Science and ICT to the Minister of Science and ICT.
Upon receipt of an application under paragraph (3), the Minister of Science and ICT may, if necessary, request assistance from the Korea Internet and Security Agency under Article 52 of the Act on Promotion of Information and Communication Network Utilization and Information Protection (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Internet and Security Agency") to determine whether to select the application, and obtain opinions from the applicant or experts and others with abundant knowledge and experience in electronic signatures.
Where the Minister of Science and ICT reviews an application under paragraph (3) and recognizes that the body meets the selection criteria under paragraph (1), he or she shall issue a certificate of selection as an assessment body in the form prescribed by the Ministry of Science and ICT Ordinance and publicly announce the fact in the Official Gazette or on the website of the Ministry.

